-- =====================================================================
-- Session 155 — Matt 21 extras-tier cross-references (single chapter)
-- =====================================================================
-- Adds Matt 21's extras-tier rows + threads to the cross-reference
-- corpus. Continues the S131 (Matt 1-2) -> S146 (Matt 16) -> S154
-- (Matt 17) extras-tier coverage; Matt 21 lands as the triumphal-entry
-- + temple-cleansing + cursed-fig-tree + authority-challenge +
-- parable-of-the-two-sons + FRAMEWORK-MAJOR parable-of-the-wicked-
-- husbandmen chapter. Per _MATTHEW_REBUILD_PAIRING_GUIDE.md, Matt 21
-- ships SOLO — antichrist-system territory, framework-dense, with the
-- kingdom-stewardship-transferred-to-the-bringing-forth-fruit-remnant
-- substance at v.43 carrying Red Line #7's seed-distinction and Red
-- Line #11's gathering-of-the-paternal-blood-remnant-of-all-twelve-
-- tribes architecture in one verse. Five framework-bearing narrative
-- movements anchor the chapter:
--
--   (a) the triumphal-entry at vv.1-11 — the King-of-Yashar''el
--       (Israel) coming-to-his-city on the foal-of-an-ass per
--       Zecharyah (Zechariah) 9:9; the meekness-substance per the
--       King''s-own-kingdom-citizens'' substance at Matthew 5:5 and
--       claimed for himself at Matthew 11:29; the multitudes crying
--       *Hoshia-na (Hosanna) to the Son of David: Blessed is he that
--       cometh in the name of Yahuah (the LORD)* from the pilgrim-
--       Hallel substance of Tehillim (Psalm) 118:25-26; the city''s
--       *Who is this?* and the multitude''s *the prophet of Natsareth
--       (Nazareth) of Galil (Galilee)* preserving the Isaiah 9:1-2
--       Galilean-light substance Matthew 4:13-16 had laid; the entry
--       lands within the Tanakh-prophesied-substance per Matthew''s
--       signature-citation formula.
--   (b) the temple-cleansing at vv.12-17 — the King''s-substantial-
--       prophetic-action against the Pharisaic-Sadducean leadership''s
--       monetization of the Court-of-the-goyim (Gentiles); the
--       Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 56:7 *my house shall be called the house
--       of prayer* citation (whose context names the outcasts-of-
--       Yashar'' el being-gathered-to-the-holy-mountain — the gathering
--       of the scattered-seed-coming-home, NOT the categorical-
--       inclusion of unrelated-nations) + the Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah)
--       7:11 *den of thieves* citation (whose context is one of the
--       Tanakh''s most-substantial Temple-judgment-passages, walking
--       the same substance against the Second-Temple leadership the
--       prophet had walked at the First-Temple); the healing of the
--       blind-and-the-lame in the Temple reversing the rabbinic-
--       substance reading of 2 Samuel 5:8 as a categorical-exclusion;
--       the children-in-the-Temple crying *Hoshia-na (Hosanna) to the
--       Son of David* with the King citing Tehillim (Psalm) 8:2 *out
--       of the mouth of babes and sucklings*; the King lodging at
--       Beit-Anyah (Bethany) — *the house of poverty* — not in the
--       city the system controls.
--   (c) the cursing-of-the-fig-tree at vv.18-22 — the substantial-
--       prophetic-action against the leaves-without-fruit substance
--       the Pharisaic-Sadducean leadership had walked; the Tanakh-
--       fig-tree-substance of Hosea 9:10, Jeremiah 8:13, Joel 1:7,
--       Micah 7:1 carried-forward as the covenant-fruitfulness-
--       substance the leadership-substance had-corrupted; the
--       framework reads the substance carefully — the substance the
--       King-walks-against is the LEADERSHIP-substance, NOT the
--       people-of-Yashar''el (Israel) categorically, per the same
--       diagnostic the matt-13 tares, the matt-15 blind-leaders-of-
--       the-blind, and the matt-23 seven-woes hold throughout the
--       gospel; the faith-and-mountain-moving teaching extending
--       Matthew 17:20''s mustard-seed-faith substance as qualitative-
--       not-quantitative.
--   (d) the parable-of-the-two-sons at vv.28-32 — the doing-of-the-
--       Father''s-will substance against the saying-yes-without-doing
--       substance; the first-son-substance saying *I will not* and-
--       afterward-repenting-and-going (the publicans-and-harlots-
--       substance walking the substance the system had-categorically-
--       excluded); the second-son-substance saying *I go, sir* (the
--       *Lord, Lord* substance per Matthew 7:21) and-walking-not (the
--       chief-priests-and-elders walking the substance of saying-yes-
--       without-doing); the substance directly ties to Matthew 7:21-23
--       (*not every one that saith unto me, Lord, Lord, shall enter
--       into the kingdom of heaven; but he that doeth the will of my
--       Father which is in heaven*) and to *Torah-lessness* (Greek
--       *anomia* — Torah-less-walking) the King names directly; the
--       apostle Ya''aqov (James) restates the substance throughout
--       his epistle (1:22, 2:14-26); the apostle Paul at Romans 2:13
--       (*not the hearers of the law are just before Elohim (God),
--       but the doers of the law shall be justified*); the apostle
--       Yochanan (John) at 1 John 2:3-4 (*hereby we do know that we
--       know him, if we keep his commandments*).
--   (e) the FRAMEWORK-MAJOR parable-of-the-wicked-husbandmen at
--       vv.33-46 — the Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 5:1-7 vineyard-of-Yahuah
--       Tseva''ot (LORD of hosts) substance walked-out at the
--       leadership-level (the husbandmen are the LEADERSHIP-substance,
--       NOT the people-of-Yashar''el (Israel) categorically — the same
--       distinction the chapter holds throughout); the servants-
--       substance is the prophets-substance the Tanakh names
--       (Jeremiah 7:25, Nehemiah 9:26); the killing-and-stoning is
--       the Tanakh-prophet-killing-pattern (Zecharyah-ben-Yehoyada at
--       2 Chronicles 24:20-22, Uriyahu at Jeremiah 26:20-23, Yirmeyahu
--       at Jeremiah 38:6); the *last of all he sent unto them his
--       son* substance is the substance the apostle Paul names at
--       Hebrews 1:1-2; the *cast him out of the vineyard, and slew
--       him* prefigures the apostle Paul''s *Yahusha (Jesus) also...
--       suffered without the gate* at Hebrews 13:12; the King citing
--       Tehillim (Psalm) 118:22-23 *the stone which the builders
--       rejected* (the same Hallel-Psalm the multitudes and the
--       children had cried-from at vv.9 and 15-16) carries the
--       stone-substance the Tanakh-prophets had laid (Genesis 28:18-
--       22, 1 Samuel 7:12, Isaiah 8:14, Isaiah 28:16, Daniel 2:34-35,
--       Zechariah 3:9, Zechariah 4:7); the chapter-pivot at v.43 —
--       *the kingdom of Elohim (God) shall be taken from you, and
--       given to a nation bringing forth the fruits thereof* — is
--       the framework-MAJOR-substance for the kingdom-stewardship-
--       transferred-from-the-current-leadership-stewards-of-Yahudah
--       (Judah) to-the-bringing-forth-fruit-remnant-of-the-gathering-
--       of-the-scattered-seed-of-both-houses-of-Yashar''el (Israel),
--       with the Greek *ethnos* SINGULAR-not-plural lockingthe
--       reading against the inherited-Christian-replacement-theology
--       collapse (the *nation* is the bringing-forth-fruit-remnant
--       of the twelve-tribes-restoration-architecture per Matthew
--       19:28 + Acts 26:6-7 + James 1:1 + Revelation 7:4-8 + 21:12-14
--       + Ephesians 2:20 + 1 Peter 2:9-10 + Hosea 1:10''s *Lo-Ammi*
--       becoming *sons of the living Elohim (God)* substance — NOT
--       the categorical-displacement of Yashar''el by the church).
--
-- The extras-library adds five framework-bearing thread-clusters
-- anchored to the five narrative-movements above:
--   Thread 1: Davidic-Messianic-King meek-and-on-the-foal at the
--     entry — the Testaments of the XII Patriarchs (Test. Yahudah
--     ch 15)''s sceptre-of-the-kingdom + rod-of-righteousness
--     substance (the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the
--     Tanakh-Tsemach-Branch-Messianic-King substance) + 2 Maccabees
--     10:7''s branches-and-palms-and-psalms substance (the Hanukkah
--     temple-rededication ceremony walking the same Sukkot-pilgrim-
--     branches-substance the multitudes walk at the entry) +
--     Sirach 36:14''s *fill Sion with thy unspeakable oracles*
--     substance (the wisdom-stream''s prayer-for-the-glory-to-fill-
--     Tsion the King''s-arrival walks-out).
--   Thread 2: Temple-cleansing — 1 Maccabees 4:43''s cleansed-the-
--     sanctuary-and-bare-out-the-defiled-stones substance + 2
--     Maccabees 10:3''s cleansed-the-temple-and-made-another-altar
--     substance (the Hanukkah temple-cleansing as the architectural-
--     parallel the chapter''s temple-cleansing walks-the-same-pattern
--     of; the cleansing-by-Yahudah-Maqqavi (Judas Maccabeus) walked
--     the same substance against the abomination-of-desolation the
--     Antiochene-system had placed in the Temple — the King-substance
--     now walks the same substance against the Pharisaic-Sadducean
--     monetization that has-displaced the substance of prayer the
--     Court-of-the-goyim was-meant-for) + Sirach 35:12''s do-not-
--     think-to-corrupt-with-gifts substance (the wisdom-stream''s
--     direct articulation against the substance of the monetization
--     the King-overturns-the-tables-of) + 1 Maccabees 4:46''s *until
--     there should come a prophet to shew what should be done with
--     them* substance (the wisdom-stream''s explicit naming of the
--     prophet-yet-to-come the King-walks-out at the entry-pericope).
--   Thread 3: Cursed-fig-tree as judgment-on-the-leaves-without-fruit
--     substance — Wisdom of Solomon 4:4-5''s flourish-in-branches-
--     for-a-time-but-standing-not-last + imperfect-branches-broken-
--     off-their-fruit-unprofitable substance (the wisdom-stream''s
--     direct verbal-anchor for the unfruitful-branches-substance the
--     King-walks-against) + Sirach 23:25''s *her children shall not
--     take root, and her branches shall bring forth no fruit*
--     substance (the wisdom-stream''s no-root-no-fruit-substance the
--     fig-tree-without-fruit walks-into) + 1 Enoch 89:35''s *Lord of
--     the sheep was silent, and the beasts and birds devoured the
--     sheep, and the sheep were scattered* substance (the Animal-
--     Apocalypse''s articulation of the consequences-on-the-flock
--     when the unfruitful-leadership-substance walks).
--   Thread 4: Parable-of-the-two-sons — the wisdom-stream''s
--     repentance-and-hypocrisy architecture — Sirach 17:24-25''s *to
--     them that repent he granted them return; return to Yahuah, and
--     forsake your sins* substance (the wisdom-stream''s direct
--     anchor for the first-son-substance saying-no-and-afterward-
--     repenting-and-doing) + Sirach 1:28-29''s come-not-to-him-with-
--     a-double-heart + be-not-an-hypocrite-in-the-sight-of-men
--     substance (the wisdom-stream''s direct anchor for the second-
--     son''s-substance saying-yes-with-the-mouth-but-walking-not) +
--     Sirach 21:1''s *have you sinned? do so no more, but ask pardon
--     for your former sins* substance + 2 Esdras 9:11''s *they that
--     have loathed my law, while they had yet liberty, and, when as
--     yet place of repentance was open to them, understood not, but
--     despised it* substance (the wisdom-stream''s direct anchor for
--     the chief-priests-and-elders-substance walking the second-
--     son''s-substance of saying-yes-and-walking-not).
--   Thread 5 (FRAMEWORK-MAJOR): Wicked-husbandmen / kingdom-given-
--     to-a-nation-bringing-forth-fruit — 2 Esdras 1:32''s *I sent to
--     you my servants the prophets, whom you have taken and slain*
--     substance (the wisdom-stream''s direct verbal-anchor for the
--     servants-killed-and-stoned substance the parable walks-out at
--     vv.34-36) + 2 Esdras 1:33''s *your house is desolate* substance
--     (the wisdom-stream''s direct verbal-anchor for the consequence-
--     substance the *cast him out of the vineyard, and slew him* of
--     v.39 walks-into per the Olivet-discourse-substance at Matthew
--     24:1-2) + 1 Enoch 89:45''s *shepherds who had not fed the sheep
--     were judged, and cast into the same fiery abyss with the
--     beasts* substance (the Animal-Apocalypse''s direct articulation
--     of the leadership-judgment-substance the *he will miserably
--     destroy those wicked men* of v.41 walks-into) + Sirach 36:11''s
--     *gather all the tribes of Ya''aqov (Jacob) together, and
--     inherit you them, as from the beginning* substance (THE direct
--     wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the kingdom-given-to-a-nation-
--     bringing-forth-fruit substance at v.43 per Red Line #11''s
--     ingathering-of-the-paternal-blood-remnant-of-all-twelve-tribes
--     architecture — the *nation* of v.43 is the gathered-twelve-
--     tribes-of-Ya''aqov the wisdom-stream''s-prayer at Sirach 36
--     names the substance for, the bringing-forth-fruit-remnant of
--     the twelve-tribes-restoration architecture per Matthew 19:28
--     + Acts 26:6-7 + James 1:1 + Revelation 7:4-8 + Ephesians 2:20
--     + 1 Peter 2:9-10, NOT the categorical-displacement of Yashar''el
--     by the church).
--
-- Historical-witness editions (Josephus, M.R. James''s apocryphal NT,
-- Lightfoot''s Apostolic Fathers) remain deferred from V1 cross-refs
-- per the historical-witness one-way rule. Jubilees, Jasher, Adam-Eve
-- Conflict, Apocalypse of Abraham, and Sonnini''s Acts of Paul do not
-- surface framework-bearing Matt 21 connections at S155 — Jubilees''
-- chronology-substance is upstream of the gospel-pivot, Jasher walks
-- the patriarchal-substance, Adam-Eve Conflict and Apocalypse of
-- Abraham bear on Genesis-substance, and Sonnini''s Acts of Paul is
-- the post-resurrection lost-sheep-mission extension not bearing on
-- Matt 21''s pre-passion narrative. The lookup view retains the S154
-- edition set for forward compatibility.
--
-- Five PROPOSED threads at extras-tier:
--   1. `davidic-messianic-king-meek-on-the-foal-in-testaments-xii-and-2-maccabees`             (sort 327)
--   2. `temple-cleansing-and-the-maccabean-rededication-architecture`                          (sort 328)
--   3. `leaves-without-fruit-judged-in-wisdom-of-solomon-sirach-and-1-enoch`                   (sort 329)
